# Secrets Baseline File
# This file documents known "secrets" that are actually false positives
# Used by secret scanning tools to prevent repeated alerts

# Last Updated: 2026-02-06
# Repository: alexanderbkl/onfleet-active-tasks

# =============================================================================
# DOCUMENTED FALSE POSITIVES
# =============================================================================

# 1. Variable names in source code (not actual secrets)
#    Files: frontend/src/store/useStore.js, backend/server.js
#    Pattern: apiKey: '', password: ''
#    Reason: Empty string initialization, not actual credentials

# 2. Documentation examples
#    Files: README.md, SECURITY_RECOMMENDATIONS.md
#    Pattern: Code examples showing how to handle API keys
#    Reason: Educational/documentation purposes only

# 3. .env.example template
#    File: .env.example
#    Pattern: Environment variable names (PORT, VITE_API_URL)
#    Reason: Template file with no actual values

# =============================================================================
# VERIFICATION NOTES
# =============================================================================

# VERIFIED CLEAN:
# ✓ No hardcoded API keys found
# ✓ No committed .env files with actual values
# ✓ No private keys or certificates
# ✓ No OAuth tokens or session secrets
# ✓ Git history contains no leaked credentials
# ✓ localStorage usage documented with security warnings

# KNOWN PATTERNS (Safe):
# - apiKey variable declarations (empty strings)
# - password field in axios auth (empty string for Onfleet API)
# - Documentation/README code examples
# - .env.example template values

# =============================================================================
# EXCLUSIONS FOR SECRET SCANNERS
# =============================================================================

# Files to exclude from secret scanning (documentation/examples):
# - README.md (contains code examples)
# - SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md (audit documentation)
# - SECURITY_RECOMMENDATIONS.md (security guidance)
# - .env.example (template file)
# - CONTRIBUTING.md (contribution guidelines)

# Patterns to allow (legitimate code patterns):
# - apiKey: '' (empty initialization)
# - password: '' (Onfleet API auth format)
# - process.env.* (environment variable usage)
# - YOUR_API_KEY (placeholder text)
# - example.com (example domains)
# - localhost (development URLs)

